  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the straight lines\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& L_1: x-y=1 \\\\\n& L_2: x+y=1 \\\\\n& L_3: 2 x+2 y=5 \\\\\n& L_4: 2 x-2 y=7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe correct statement is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ycnWB",
      "text": "\n$L_1\\left\\|L_4, L_2\\right\\| L_3, L_1$ intersect $L_4$.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tuSho",
      "text": "\n$L_1 \\perp L_2, L_1 \\| L_3, L_1$ intersect $L_2$.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VyCMS",
      "text": "\n$L_1 \\perp L_2, L_2 \\| L_3, L_1$ intersect $L_4$.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jpmQw",
      "text": "\n$L_1 \\perp L_2, L_1 \\perp L_3, L_2$ intersect $L_4$.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
